 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505789,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate <span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{7}{{12}}\">\\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{7}{{12}}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{7}{{12}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find the LCM of 9 and 12. (You can use Desmos to do this.)</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Number</td>\n<td>Factors</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>LCM</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{LCM}} = 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 \\times 3 = 36\"></span></p>\n<p>Rewrite the fractions with 36 as the denominator.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{4 \\times 4}}{{9 \\times 4}} + \\frac{{7 \\times 3}}{{12 \\times 3}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{16}}{{36}} + \\frac{{21}}{{36}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Now, you can add the fractions by adding the numerators.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{37}}{{36}}\"></span></p>\n<p>There are no common factors to divide out.</p>\n<p>Alternative answer: <span data-math=\"1\\frac{1}{{36}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{{37}}{{36}}\">\\frac{{37}}{{36}}</span>"
    }
   ],
